
==================================================
  FUNCTION TABLE CALCULATOR (Variant 3) - MAIN MENU
==================================================
 This program calculates the function y(x) for every x
 from a start value to an end value with a chosen step and shows a table:
   y = 1/(2x) + product(i + x), i = 1..n-2                 if x < 3
   y = product(j = 1..n) of sum(i = 1..n+3) (i + 1/(4j^2))   if x >= 3
--------------------------------------------------
 Current data: not entered yet (choose 1 or 2)
--------------------------------------------------
 1. Enter data from keyboard  - type the start, end, step and n
 2. Load data from file       - read the same 4 values from a file
 3. Calculate and show table  - build the table of y(x), save it if needed
 4. Help                      - meaning of every value, rules, examples
 0. Exit                      - close the program
 Choose an option (0-4): 
==================================================
  ENTER DATA FROM KEYBOARD
==================================================
 The table shows y for every x from the start value to the end value,
 moving by the step. Example: start -2, end 4, step 1 gives
 x = -2, -1, 0, 1, 2, 3, 4.

 Start value of x (where the table begins, e.g. -2):  End value of x (where the table ends, not smaller than the start, e.g. 4):  Step (how much x grows in each row, greater than 0, e.g. 1):  Parameter n (the last number the formula counts up to: 1, 2, ... n; whole number from 4 to 1000, e.g. 5): 
 Data accepted: x from -1 to 1, step 0.25, n = 6

 Press Enter to continue...
